tests/diagnostics/front/precedence_prefix.n:5:15: error N00B-P0036: `not` followed by `==` is not allowed, because this could be read more than one way
  help: add parentheses to say which one you mean:
    5 | let negated = (not p) == q
    5 | let negated = not (p == q)
tests/diagnostics/front/precedence_prefix.n:6:14: error N00B-P0036: `!` followed by `==` is not allowed, because this could be read more than one way
  help: add parentheses to say which one you mean:
    6 | let symbol = (!p) == q
    6 | let symbol = !(p == q)
tests/diagnostics/front/precedence_prefix.n:7:15: error N00B-P0036: `cast` followed by `/` is not allowed, because this could be read more than one way
  help: add parentheses to say which one you mean:
    7 | let divided = cast[f64](a) / 2.0
    7 | let divided = cast[f64](a / 2.0)
tests/diagnostics/front/precedence_prefix.n:8:15: error N00B-P0036: `unsafe_cast` followed by `+` is not allowed, because this could be read more than one way
  help: add parentheses to say which one you mean:
    8 | let widened = unsafe_cast[i64](a) + 1
    8 | let widened = unsafe_cast[i64](a + 1)
tests/diagnostics/front/precedence_prefix.n:9:18: error N00B-P0036: `ref` followed by `+` is not allowed, because this could be read more than one way
  help: add parentheses to say which one you mean:
